%
% A TSTP derivation produced by OUR OWN reasoner — no external prover was
% involved. Source problem:
%   conformance/logic/cases/external/tptp-mini/theorem-subclass/source/problem.p
%   (a ⊑ b, b ⊑ c ⊢ a ⊑ c; SZS status Theorem)
%
% How it was produced:
%   1. `gmeow_conformance::external::tptp::parse_tptp` parses the problem.
%   2. `gmeow_conformance::external::tptp::lower_to_fol_program` reduces the
%      refutation `premises ∧ ¬conjecture` into the Horn fragment: the conjecture
%      ∀X.(a(X) → c(X)) is negated through the shared `gmeow_logic::entail::negate`
%      waist, whose fresh reserved-namespace witness w yields the asserted fact
%      a(w) and the goal c(w).
%   3. `gmeow_logic::proof_tree::prove_reasoning_program` resolves that goal with
%      the PurRDF proof-carrying SLG-WFS backward engine
%      (`purrdf::datalog::resolve_fol`) and VALIDATES every answer's proof term
%      with PurRDF's Curry–Howard checker
%      (`purrdf::datalog::resolve_fol::check_fol_proof`), which independently
%      re-derives each conclusion from its premises.
%   4. `ProofTree::to_tstp` projects the checked proof term to the lines below.
%
% The derivation of c(w) from a(w) IS the refutation: it contradicts the negated
% conjecture's ¬c(w).
%
% Reading the surface:
%   * Each step name `d_<hex>` is the exact image of that step's content-addressed
%     derivation IRI, `https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/derivation/<hex>`,
%     where `<hex>` is PurRDF's `derivation_id` — a SHA-1 over the proof's rule
%     identity and its recursive sub-proof digests. gmeow derives the IRI from
%     PurRDF's content digest; PurRDF itself mints no IRIs.
%   * Predicates, constants, and inference-rule identities are IRIs, so they ride
%     as TPTP single-quoted atoms rather than being lossily shortened.
%   * An `inference(...)` rule IRI names the fired clause's content-addressed
%     identity (`.../gmeow/goal-directed/rule/<blake3>`, a blake3 digest of
%     PurRDF's `rule_identity`), which is what the proof checker re-derives against.
%   * Leaves are `axiom` (asserted EDB facts); derived steps are `plain`.
cnf(d_b17bff2379a308d9d6b50b0f9a073ef5e051b853, axiom, 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tptp#a'('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entail/reserved#witness-d4a1e02579180296')).
cnf(d_0e9d1c683cc59b3da5626f16bd835a646aefd1ac, plain, 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tptp#b'('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entail/reserved#witness-d4a1e02579180296'), inference('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/goal-directed/rule/c4baaa462517cae869dfedd50b8efef4afaf2fe9037b1f0c4f5e520f9200ffdf', [status(thm)], [d_b17bff2379a308d9d6b50b0f9a073ef5e051b853])).
cnf(d_2f2cb9320e4a9d0302cb5797a1e21f10d26a3e26, plain, 'https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/tptp#c'('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/entail/reserved#witness-d4a1e02579180296'), inference('https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/goal-directed/rule/772035b62784cf12dce87129ba59bf14365477017a1c8c5fed58ada7d4ad35be', [status(thm)], [d_0e9d1c683cc59b3da5626f16bd835a646aefd1ac])).
